# I. Corporate profile

# Main battalion business

James Hardie Industries is the world’s largest manufacturer of fibre cement products, based in Dublin, Ireland, and listed mainly on the New York Stock Exchange (JHX) and the Australian Stock Exchange (JHX.AX). Companies produce and sell fibre-cement exterior walls, housing materials and other construction products, mainly for new construction and renovation of residential buildings.

In July 2025, the company completed the acquisition of AZEK with $8.75 billion, significantly expanding into the area of outdoor living, including composite material decks, rails and ornamental products.

